# No Tooltips on Intent Chips

Intent chips must **never** have a tooltip, by any means. The label on the
chip is already the message. This is a permanent, non-negotiable design rule
— especially in the chat module.

## What is banned

- The shared hover card (`#lir-tooltip` / `js/lir-tooltip.js`) on an intent chip
- A native browser `title` bubble
- A `data-tip` (or any other hover-card attribute) on the chip
- A CSS-only tip (`::after`, `[title]:hover`, etc.) on the chip
- Re-adding `.ws-intent-chip`, `.sc-reply-chips .chip`, `.sc-inline-chips .chip`,
  `.ws-chips .chip`, or `.chip-dive` to the tooltip allow-list

## What still gets a tooltip

Icon-only controls (nav, module header, composer send, …) and data/status
chips (Shield / GRAS pills via `chip-tooltip.js`) keep their hover cards.
Those are not intent chips.

## How it is wired

`js/wiseai-chat.js` renders chips with no `title` and no `data-tip`.
`js/lir-tooltip.js` skips intent chips and strips a leftover native `title`
on hover so a stray attribute cannot surface a bubble.

## Rules for the agent

- Never put `title` or `data-tip` on an intent chip.
- Never wire an intent chip into the shared tooltip selector.
- A longer ask / description is not a hover caption — it belongs in the
  transcript when the chip is tapped, not on a card above the chip.
- `aria-label` is only for the “What can I ask?” chip, whose visible text is
  aria-hidden shimmer. Regular chips use their visible label.
